{
  "about": "Which permission rule decides (permission/rules.md, spec 3.8.0). The rules by layer: `defaults` true — permission/defaults.json as the `default` layer; `user` and `project` — a configuration's permission map (a key's value an action, or a map of pattern → action, read in the order written); `made` — rules made during the session, in order, each `by` an `always` answer or a `menu`. With `request` (`permission`, `pattern`: what one call asks for): expect the action that decides, or null where no rule matches. With `set` (a rule a person makes now, by a menu): expect `result` — `unchanged` (the action is already in force), `refused` with the rule in its way as `by`, or `made` with `still`, the stricter narrower rules that still apply, in the order read. The same answers for a rule typed into a file as for one a menu wrote. LLeMbas: security/permission rules; CLI: src/permission/evaluate.ts.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "about": "The defaults alone: a file is read, a .env asks.",
      "defaults": true,
      "request": {
        "permission": "read",
        "pattern": "src/app.ts"
      },
      "expect": "allow"
    },
    {
      "about": "The same, for another call.",
      "defaults": true,
      "request": {
        "permission": "read",
        "pattern": "config/.env"
      },
      "expect": "ask"
    },
    {
      "about": "A project says read: allow. A broader rule made later does not unlock the narrower ask: .env still asks.",
      "defaults": true,
      "project": {
        "read": "allow"
      },
      "request": {
        "permission": "read",
        "pattern": ".env"
      },
      "expect": "ask"
    },
    {
      "about": "…and everything the broad default decided is as the project says.",
      "defaults": true,
      "project": {
        "read": "allow"
      },
      "request": {
        "permission": "read",
        "pattern": "notes.txt"
      },
      "expect": "allow"
    },
    {
      "about": "The same rule set in a menu, in the session it was made in.",
      "defaults": true,
      "made": [
        {
          "permission": "read",
          "pattern": "*",
          "action": "allow",
          "by": "menu"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "permission": "read",
        "pattern": ".env.local"
      },
      "expect": "ask"
    },
    {
      "about": "The project names the narrow thing itself: allowed.",
      "defaults": true,
      "project": {
        "read": {
          "*.env": "allow"
        }
      },
      "request": {
        "permission": "read",
        "pattern": ".env"
      },
      "expect": "allow"
    },
    {
      "about": "The broadest rule there is, made in a menu: .env still asks.",
      "defaults": true,
      "made": [
        {
          "permission": "*",
          "pattern": "*",
          "action": "allow",
          "by": "menu"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "permission": "read",
        "pattern": ".env"
      },
      "expect": "ask"
    },
    {
      "about": "web_fetch: allow in a project leaves private addresses asking.",
      "defaults": true,
      "project": {
        "web_fetch": "allow"
      },
      "request": {
        "permission": "web_fetch",
        "pattern": "private:http://127.0.0.1:8080/admin"
      },
      "expect": "ask"
    },
    {
      "about": "The same, for another call.",
      "defaults": true,
      "project": {
        "web_fetch": "allow"
      },
      "request": {
        "permission": "web_fetch",
        "pattern": "https://example.org/"
      },
      "expect": "allow"
    },
    {
      "about": "The person's own config denies rm; `bash allow` made in a menu does not undo it.",
      "defaults": true,
      "user": {
        "bash": {
          "rm *": "deny"
        }
      },
      "made": [
        {
          "permission": "bash",
          "pattern": "*",
          "action": "allow",
          "by": "menu"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "permission": "bash",
        "pattern": "rm -rf build"
      },
      "expect": "deny"
    },
    {
      "about": "…and allows what only the broad default asked about.",
      "defaults": true,
      "user": {
        "bash": {
          "rm *": "deny"
        }
      },
      "made": [
        {
          "permission": "bash",
          "pattern": "*",
          "action": "allow",
          "by": "menu"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "permission": "bash",
        "pattern": "make all"
      },
      "expect": "allow"
    },
    {
      "about": "The same from a project's file (the next start, after the menu saved it).",
      "defaults": true,
      "user": {
        "bash": {
          "rm *": "deny"
        }
      },
      "project": {
        "bash": "allow"
      },
      "request": {
        "permission": "bash",
        "pattern": "rm -rf build"
      },
      "expect": "deny"
    },
    {
      "about": "The person's own `git push *`: ask stands against a project's bash: allow.",
      "defaults": true,
      "user": {
        "bash": {
          "git push *": "ask"
        }
      },
      "project": {
        "bash": "allow"
      },
      "request": {
        "permission": "bash",
        "pattern": "git push origin main"
      },
      "expect": "ask"
    },
    {
      "about": "The person's own answer is a floor of any breadth: their bash: ask stands against a project's narrower allow.",
      "defaults": true,
      "user": {
        "bash": "ask"
      },
      "project": {
        "bash": {
          "make *": "allow"
        }
      },
      "request": {
        "permission": "bash",
        "pattern": "make all"
      },
      "expect": "ask"
    },
    {
      "about": "The person's own file is read last-match-wins, as it always was: their broad allow after the defaults does unlock .env — it is theirs to say.",
      "defaults": true,
      "user": {
        "read": "allow"
      },
      "request": {
        "permission": "read",
        "pattern": ".env"
      },
      "expect": "allow"
    },
    {
      "about": "Within a project's file too, a narrower stricter line keeps winning over a broader one written after it.",
      "project": {
        "bash": {
          "git push *": "ask",
          "*": "allow"
        }
      },
      "request": {
        "permission": "bash",
        "pattern": "git push origin main"
      },
      "expect": "ask"
    },
    {
      "about": "A project's narrow allow after its own broad deny is an exception it wrote: allowed.",
      "project": {
        "bash": {
          "*": "deny",
          "git status": "allow"
        }
      },
      "request": {
        "permission": "bash",
        "pattern": "git status"
      },
      "expect": "allow"
    },
    {
      "about": "An \"always\" answer never undoes a written deny, of any breadth.",
      "project": {
        "bash": {
          "*": "deny"
        }
      },
      "made": [
        {
          "permission": "bash",
          "pattern": "git status",
          "action": "allow",
          "by": "always"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "permission": "bash",
        "pattern": "git status"
      },
      "expect": "deny"
    },
    {
      "about": "An \"always\" answer for `git *` leaves the narrower `git push --force *`: deny.",
      "user": {
        "bash": {
          "git push --force *": "deny"
        }
      },
      "made": [
        {
          "permission": "bash",
          "pattern": "git *",
          "action": "allow",
          "by": "always"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "permission": "bash",
        "pattern": "git push --force origin main"
      },
      "expect": "deny"
    },
    {
      "about": "A stricter rule made later always decides.",
      "defaults": true,
      "made": [
        {
          "permission": "read",
          "pattern": "*",
          "action": "deny",
          "by": "menu"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "permission": "read",
        "pattern": "src/app.ts"
      },
      "expect": "deny"
    },
    {
      "about": "No rule matches: none decides (the class and the mode do).",
      "user": {
        "bash": {
          "ls *": "allow"
        }
      },
      "request": {
        "permission": "edit",
        "pattern": "a.txt"
      },
      "expect": null
    },
    {
      "about": "Choosing the action already in force changes nothing.",
      "defaults": true,
      "set": {
        "permission": "read",
        "pattern": "*",
        "action": "allow"
      },
      "expect": {
        "result": "unchanged"
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "A rule that makes something stricter is made; nothing stricter is left standing.",
      "defaults": true,
      "set": {
        "permission": "read",
        "pattern": "*",
        "action": "ask"
      },
      "expect": {
        "result": "made",
        "still": []
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "A broad allow is made, and says which stricter rules still apply.",
      "defaults": true,
      "made": [
        {
          "permission": "web_fetch",
          "pattern": "*",
          "action": "ask",
          "by": "menu"
        }
      ],
      "set": {
        "permission": "web_fetch",
        "pattern": "*",
        "action": "allow"
      },
      "expect": {
        "result": "made",
        "still": [
          {
            "permission": "web_fetch",
            "pattern": "private:*",
            "action": "ask"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "The person's own rule, loosened where it stands: refused, naming it.",
      "user": {
        "bash": {
          "git push *": "ask"
        }
      },
      "set": {
        "permission": "bash",
        "pattern": "git push *",
        "action": "allow"
      },
      "expect": {
        "result": "refused",
        "by": {
          "permission": "bash",
          "pattern": "git push *",
          "action": "ask"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "A narrower allow under a written deny: refused — the deny takes it in whole.",
      "user": {
        "bash": {
          "rm *": "deny"
        }
      },
      "set": {
        "permission": "bash",
        "pattern": "rm -rf build",
        "action": "allow"
      },
      "expect": {
        "result": "refused",
        "by": {
          "permission": "bash",
          "pattern": "rm *",
          "action": "deny"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "A broader allow over the person's narrower deny is made — and the deny still applies.",
      "user": {
        "bash": {
          "rm *": "deny"
        }
      },
      "set": {
        "permission": "bash",
        "pattern": "*",
        "action": "allow"
      },
      "expect": {
        "result": "made",
        "still": [
          {
            "permission": "bash",
            "pattern": "rm *",
            "action": "deny"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
